Reading: a cheater who wants, say, <1% chance of being caught over a round of c=100 challenges needs (1-1/k)^100 > 0.99, i.e. k > ~10000 (k>=2^14). That large k is exactly what the checkpoint timing budget (Part 4) also forces.
